        "review_notes": "The eee604db779 merge brought in upstream's size-based RBE pool routing\n(bazel/test_exec_properties.bzl): a test's Bazel size picks its pool by memory\ntier (SIZE_TO_MEMORY_MB), and size=\"large\" (7 GB) maps to\nPool=large_mem_2core_x86_64. bb-psmdb has no workers for that pool, so those\ntests fail at dispatch with FAILED_PRECONDITION: No workers exist. The prior\n-cpu:2 tag filter no longer matches them (upstream dropped cpu:n tags in favor\nof size), so it excluded nothing.\n\nFiltering by size alone did not work either: mongo_cc_test splits each test into\nan intermediate cc_test (name_with_debug, filtered out via -intermediate_debug)\nand the final_target extract_debuginfo_test that Bazel actually runs. Only the\nintermediate carried size=large; the final target inherited the pool via\nexec_properties but defaulted to size=medium, so --test_size_filters couldn't\nsee it.\n\nFix both halves:\n- mongo_src_rules.bzl: forward  to the final_target extract_debuginfo_test\n  so its size attribute matches the size that routed it to a pool (also fixes\n  its default test timeout).\n- .bazelrc.psmdb: restrict the remote unittest run to\n  --test_size_filters=small,medium. Use the inclusive form, not -large: Bazel\n  treats a negative-only size filter as an empty (ignored) set, so -large runs\n  every size. small,medium excludes large (and enormous; none exist today)."
